Water units sail to the nearest reachable water instead of refusing the order.

Ships (and amphibious units) kept the exact A* in order_unit_move while land
units got the W2-SK-05/16 nearest-reachable fallback, so any order whose goal
cell was not water-passable -- a click that landed on the shore, a pond no
route reaches, a group-formation cell that fell on land -- was refused
outright and the ship just sat still. All domains now take the same
find_path_nearest_t on their own grid (plus the same unit-cost re-search),
so a ship sails to the nearest shore of its own water body. Reachable water
orders are byte-identical (same A* body, same goal); the old "naval unit
ordered onto land is BLOCKED" case still stays put, correctly, because the
ship is already on the only reachable water cell. No save-format change.

